Where the corresponding source of the distribution packages is available
  Each apk package record in /lib/apk/db/installed names its origin and the Alpine `aports`
  commit it was built from (field `c`). At such a commit the build recipe is at
    https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/raw/<commit>/<repository>/<origin>/APKBUILD
  (checked on 2026-11-14 for openjdk11 at ea4636f2a587561db565f796e436072868024cbf, community,
  and busybox at b8f92cf12ab6e48d1c3a7a0e590521581443e720, main). The recipe lists the source
  archives; Alpine's source mirror is https://distfiles.alpinelinux.org/distfiles/<v3.11|v3.12>/
  (busybox-1.31.1.tar.bz2 present for both). The OpenJDK source is the upstream tag
  jdk-11.0.9-ga / jdk-11.0.5-ga of https://github.com/openjdk/jdk11u (both tags resolve); the
  binary packages are still served at https://dl-cdn.alpinelinux.org/alpine/<v3.11|v3.12>/
  (openjdk11-jre-headless 11.0.5_p10-r0 and 11.0.9_p11-r0 checked).
  Echo (Debian 10.6): the source packages are on snapshot.debian.org
  (https://snapshot.debian.org/mr/package/<source>/<version>/srcfiles), listed in
  /var/lib/dpkg/status of the image (Source and Version fields).

The source bundle
  The corresponding source of every package whose recorded licence includes the GPL or LGPL
  (37 Alpine source packages, 82 Debian source packages: 119 in all, 511 files, none missing)
  is collected in the release asset spinnaker-1.25.4-sources.tar (620,062,720 bytes, sha256
  b4b8e62a5fc2fc1d397ce587c25f5c209128b1bc48edc3e2c80abcb7c64d344a), released next to the images.
  It contains, per Alpine package, every file of the package's aports directory at the recorded
  commit (APKBUILD and patches) and every remote source file of its APKBUILD, each checked
  against the APKBUILD's sha512 (and the aports files against their git blob ids); per Debian
  package the .dsc, upstream tarball(s) and Debian tarball from snapshot.debian.org, checked
  against the snapshot's sha1 and the .dsc's sha256. Its first entry, MANIFEST, lists package,
  version, licence, commit or source reference, the images containing it, and every file with
  its sha512. The largest parts are the OpenJDK sources (112 MB and 86 MB), gcc-8 (84 MB) and
  glibc (17 MB). scripts/build-spinnaker-sources.py rebuilds it from packages.tsv (a second
  build from the same downloads gave a byte-identical tar); the tar holds the source as
  published, not Alpine's or Debian's binary packages. The Go binaries and Python packages
  listed above are not in it.

These images are from 2021 and receive no updates: the JVM, the libraries and OpenSSL 1.1.1
in them are unmaintained and should be assumed to have known vulnerabilities. They exist to
reproduce the behaviour of Spinnaker 1.25.4 in tests; do not run them with real credentials
or on exposed networks.
